          "ImageDescription": {
            "value": "U.S. Marines with Marine Rotational Force – Darwin 25.3 pose with a game ball during a friendly game of soccer with the senior men’s team of the Mindil Aces Football Club during a sporting event held in Darwin, Australia, March 29, 2025. The club is one of the largest single code sporting clubs in Darwin that provide a welcoming, family-oriented environment for all to enjoy playing association football within the community. MRF-D is an annual six-month rotational deployment to enhance interoperability with the Australian Defence Force and allies and partners and provide a forward-postured crisis response force in the Indo-Pacific. (U.S. Marine Corps photo by Cpl. Angelina Sara)",
            "source": "commons-desc-page"
          },
          "DateTimeOriginal": {
            "value": "Taken on 29 March 2025",
            "source": "commons-desc-page"
          },
